* Constant On-Time Lab -- educational combinational phase allocators
* Signals are normalized to 0..VLOGIC. TOKEN below 0.5 selects phase 1;
* TOKEN above 0.5 selects phase 2. An external sequencer generates TOKEN.

* ROUND_ROBIN_2 REQ1 REQ2 TOKEN INHIBIT GRANT1 GRANT2 DENIED1 DENIED2
* Only the selected phase can receive a grant. A request for the other phase is
* recorded as denied; fairness therefore depends on TOKEN advancing.
.SUBCKT ROUND_ROBIN_2 REQ1 REQ2 TOKEN INHIBIT
+ GRANT1 GRANT2 DENIED1 DENIED2 PARAMS: VLOGIC=1
ENR1 NR1 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(REQ1)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ENR2 NR2 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(REQ2)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ENTOK NTOK 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(TOKEN)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ENENA NENA 0 VALUE={1-LIMIT(V(INHIBIT)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
EG1 GRANT1 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR1)*(1-V(NTOK))*V(NENA)}
EG2 GRANT2 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR2)*V(NTOK)*V(NENA)}
ED1 DENIED1 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR1)*(1-V(GRANT1)/VLOGIC)}
ED2 DENIED2 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR2)*(1-V(GRANT2)/VLOGIC)}
.ENDS ROUND_ROBIN_2

* FIRST_ELIGIBLE_2 REQ1 REQ2 INHIBIT GRANT1 GRANT2 DENIED1 DENIED2
* Phase 1 has fixed priority. This intentionally demonstrates starvation risk.
.SUBCKT FIRST_ELIGIBLE_2 REQ1 REQ2 INHIBIT
+ GRANT1 GRANT2 DENIED1 DENIED2 PARAMS: VLOGIC=1
ENR1 NR1 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(REQ1)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ENR2 NR2 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(REQ2)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ENENA NENA 0 VALUE={1-LIMIT(V(INHIBIT)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
EG1 GRANT1 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR1)*V(NENA)}
EG2 GRANT2 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR2)*(1-V(NR1))*V(NENA)}
ED1 DENIED1 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR1)*(1-V(GRANT1)/VLOGIC)}
ED2 DENIED2 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR2)*(1-V(GRANT2)/VLOGIC)}
.ENDS FIRST_ELIGIBLE_2

* CURRENT_PRIORITY_2 uses sensed current plus a documented phase-1 tie bias.
* CURRENT_PRIORITY_2 REQ1 REQ2 I1 I2 INHIBIT G1 G2 D1 D2
.SUBCKT CURRENT_PRIORITY_2 REQ1 REQ2 I1 I2 INHIBIT
+ GRANT1 GRANT2 DENIED1 DENIED2 PARAMS:
+ VLOGIC=1 TIEBIAS=50m
ENR1 NR1 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(REQ1)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ENR2 NR2 0 VALUE={LIMIT(V(REQ2)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
ENENA NENA 0 VALUE={1-LIMIT(V(INHIBIT)/VLOGIC,0,1)}
* Compute one Boolean winner, then derive its exact complement. Phase 1 wins
* the exact boundary and whenever I1-I2 <= TIEBIAS; phase 2 wins only above it.
* TIEBIAS therefore provides a deterministic phase-1 preference near equality.
EWIN1 WIN1 0 VALUE={IF(V(I1)-V(I2)>TIEBIAS,0,1)}
EWIN2 WIN2 0 VALUE={1-V(WIN1)}
EG1 GRANT1 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NENA)*V(NR1)*
+ (1-V(NR2)+V(NR2)*V(WIN1))}
EG2 GRANT2 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NENA)*V(NR2)*
+ (1-V(NR1)+V(NR1)*V(WIN2))}
ED1 DENIED1 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR1)*(1-V(GRANT1)/VLOGIC)}
ED2 DENIED2 0 VALUE={VLOGIC*V(NR2)*(1-V(GRANT2)/VLOGIC)}
.ENDS CURRENT_PRIORITY_2
